  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:d1a80202e9672efe1b7382408b4c20dda1026c5ea71377ae0318782c5037ab14",
      "text": "In the NT-0796 phase 1b study, 10 subjects with PD received 150 mg open-label NT-0796 every 12 h for 28 days. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40792655/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.alzforum.org/news/conference-coverage/nlrp3-inhibitor-passes-muster-early-parkinsons-trial"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:0aaf2546197203c1d8db5635511b229c5d3a1993dd328aae360f445a73b2330f",
        "ev:9a86b44212b361e8eebef4714262a62d5d9bbf4c4b7c52674d601007683bc56c"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:5e26795482d135594dc94cdc4de81d37a7ccf8d97fddef3e366a35151d5da0a3",
      "text": "A news report on a conference presentation says that in Roche's selnoflast study in Parkinson's disease, the inflammasome-driven cytokine response in lipopolysaccharide-treated blood samples was down by about 90 percent from study start and IL-18 in cerebrospinal fluid had fallen by about 30 percent on day 28, with no differences in the placebo group. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-03-27)",
      "source_url": "https://www.alzforum.org/news/conference-coverage/nlrp3-inhibitor-passes-muster-early-parkinsons-trial",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:4fb0828ca834e96caca97c053efb31493bdcfd57d4532709abbf7c12e885b696"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:220e67d18d3a32dcc71e7e75735d6d606d8676b27239e1e2589e4161f342671f",
      "text": "Dapansutrile, described as having a highly specific effect on the NLRP3 inflammasome, is in a Phase 2 trial in Parkinson's disease registered as NCT07157735 with status RECRUITING and an estimated 36 participants. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
      "source_url": "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT07157735",
      "also": [
        "https://cureparkinsons.org.uk/2026/02/results-from-the-phase-2-aza-pd-trial-are-now-published/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:19f53c4170829a8164934bbb8a5787d2c7bb3065e521c08a55463a401ce2347d",
        "ev:4091c46d5463361e032c8c0e26a31db3bc806fce4bd8fa4cdeaf812df7f4da27",
        "ev:a5346f99e1d94b048ca27384d933af28406a3fe87918956bd45fa9dfb5c7ba78",
        "ev:a70468006462ae8cd289302c2005cfb00b1c04fdc7d5b12e0e97ac3dac8987d7",
        "ev:aa2c52e65782fb88a4bdedd3669cef1923ea616a385d850f96160ac887709288",
        "ev:f116aa17a4d1ac93c0902364944b0004f904af2f2c9f8c3a14b73d2c08e825bf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:856fd1a786f211782ecb38dc7953fdbd2ad2db5ba3686c856136f0005158b261",
      "text": "A news report on a conference presentation says selnoflast motor outcomes were exploratory: MDS-UPDRS Part III improved by two to three points in the selnoflast group versus worsening by a point or less on placebo, and average differences were small and not statistically significant. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-03-27)",
      "source_url": "https://www.alzforum.org/news/conference-coverage/nlrp3-inhibitor-passes-muster-early-parkinsons-trial",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:e783c02103356261696c1cd4025e4edce45d402da606e320ef75fa87372fb5ae"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:bb868277db1a3a6a39a04dded783fec3d65450bf1a006e92e39693f3607b1412",
      "text": "A review reports that in sargramostim, a recombinant GMCSF, undergoing extended phase 1 testing, initial results with 8 weeks of treatment in 20 patients with PD showed increased numbers and suppressive function of peripheral T regulatory cells and a modest reduction in UPDRS part III scores versus the placebo arm. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11492043/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:4e81c48da52faafb2f378b6f754303345ed5636198cffa458b0b25b5f7867dca"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:536835ec5f769861c1eb84d3029546e7833a66c772a614708c6583c3c05fbbcb",
      "text": "Reviews report that \u03b1-synuclein can drive NLRP3 inflammasome activation in microglia, and that inflammasome activation releases pro-inflammatory cytokines. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11492043/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12916702/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:5fff88a0c00cca8a949061edebe0a231aed46f361b70841e0e43d83c53881282",
        "ev:7a1c96680cc10926d182ffc512a66aa880f82f851b6d0b04a6786a5cbce98bd6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:c675cebb6f213bca23945c0bddbca4bd25a7a20c4aeaa9bac8404ea5e8781cc9",
      "text": "The authors report that NT-0796 drove reductions in systemic inflammatory markers including high-sensitivity C-reactive protein, fibrinogen and IL-18, and reductions in neuroinflammation within the CNS of subjects with PD. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-03-27)",
      "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40792655/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.alzforum.org/news/conference-coverage/nlrp3-inhibitor-passes-muster-early-parkinsons-trial"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:455e67f2e636ba1cf92019fc26c1a3741455fa98bfdf146b550afb5625d5e7d2",
        "ev:89fea25e12df082648006a9131952cf9f1fdc2ea78f722d3b3dbf35d73b873f2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:b9ed9184d62e165bd921ee46cbe4120fe9ca2817007c2b6ca11cbb46c9e6af23",
      "text": "The NT-0796 phase 1b study was designed to assess safety, tolerability, pharmacokinetics and anti-inflammatory effects, and a news report on the work states that motor outcomes were not assessed. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40792655/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.alzforum.org/news/conference-coverage/nlrp3-inhibitor-passes-muster-early-parkinsons-trial"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:b743b3e4a3a2bce7532e65e8d695d7a5ac3b935af9f1bcbdc3f1522b1bdc8b35",
        "ev:daf5090bb5dee9946e3d138d04e6e70c4e1563c28001288c71e54e1fe3e884ef"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:4b2950169289220c644e584718acbf982434491c9c3ed19aef55890cbc261a05",
      "text": "The VENT-02 Parkinson's study registered as NCT06822517 lists incidence of treatment-emergent adverse events (TEAEs) as its primary outcome, and its congress abstract states the primary endpoint is safety. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
      "source_url": "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT06822517",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mdsabstracts.org/abstract/a-randomized-double-blind-placebo-controlled-phase-2-study-of-the-nlrp3-inhibitor-vent-02-in-patients-with-mild-to-moderate-parkinsons-disease/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:54d3be47fd6d418520a5c7b646f1e5074e75f3f847e869b4d7b57b36966313f0",
        "ev:70ea3dccde8ee033ea7037a13bcf56188fda6d1773dd66684748dafbcbec25e6",
        "ev:c8ea5f0de299b2ef19e0e142883ba63dadbca9ecd08877800bf647483fdee447"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:9b61dabb2d00eb2b476999347fc74d09a19a3855cf0dc5ab5af3f06b0707127f",
      "text": "Sources differ on the VENT-02 Parkinson's study: the congress abstract and sponsor page describe a Phase 2 program with 30 patients, while registry record NCT06822517 titles it Phase 1b and lists status TERMINATED with 29 enrolled. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mdsabstracts.org/abstract/a-randomized-double-blind-placebo-controlled-phase-2-study-of-the-nlrp3-inhibitor-vent-02-in-patients-with-mild-to-moderate-parkinsons-disease/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.ventustx.com/pipeline/nlrp3/",
        "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT06822517"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:6a1e36c0dcd31ce24541be508e155877bbdfdda741c9cece53e55df1f9007f15",
        "ev:6d04159f7ace71469a0121d1b7d2b0d4d519f0c9def3be2c308daaac0bbe7fa6",
        "ev:a8384fb7799e2afd4d87fc5fbd14933297618a868d0abcd720109a2d33ac57c0",
        "ev:a8cb7d8574dc9cea21510bc8e53bded3fc38fe7e1fe707a4660ba81c83eb756c",
        "ev:bbdaaa6613cc4e5a30f68835a55d876b931d8e54aa431c15f9520cac2c50c05b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:c65fb7706884005b06d07aa21c586057e77a219ebd6b4dc00e4f4bcab3996057",
      "text": "Roche's NCT05924243 study of RO7486967 in early idiopathic PD is registered as a Phase 1b, adaptive, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled study with registry status COMPLETED. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
      "source_url": "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT05924243",
      "also": [
        "https://www.isrctn.com/ISRCTN85338453"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:10a9059e5ba8a924b910330c40fdbcb00720eeab732892cbd9c5667e800df4da",
        "ev:1c316a9b866b76f048a1cc76fa6a50c46b55733fa0885301027051fafb399ace",
        "ev:5494d796f35b5e5f0191f5d58ef13bc831a9974508f4971b139b83965dd80d51",
        "ev:dbd56e7649662a67769e33a449e364c56dc4c3bd7e8ba3365d6d487aeb949915"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:452f94e2cf349ddfe03e32ef7c28e91b545a3dcf28594f637346d04224328a6d",
      "text": "In the AZA-PD randomised, placebo-controlled phase 2 trial (66 randomly assigned: azathioprine n=32, placebo n=34), the primary outcome, change in MDS-UPDRS gait-axial score in the off-state at 12 months, was not met. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
      "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41389828/",
      "also": [
        "https://cureparkinsons.org.uk/2026/02/results-from-the-phase-2-aza-pd-trial-are-now-published/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:285e3ec843b3fbddc28b08d07e6bd56ac14a08c78f5339512d3f5839f34e9d6d",
        "ev:3d979e39faf788d061f9aa2c3910aba5eb3934082ca42245353661d40b0817a8",
        "ev:8aef87678a7f014577b76609c7fa4590e1dc034e21705c68f6c52bf47e4b604c",
        "ev:a5c81d23923dd1b9403c06bbe306aebdc99a61d20f54f98e3d5602445a163211",
        "ev:c4fe74ce89f7c342127cbb2fe0622b65d9c22a8d0f8f6d151207f06318e24876"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:92ef3a950cb074b965ef85068b11603d8be818eb8c5dd2f5669acb6fbedbfd94",
      "text": "Exploratory analyses in the azathioprine trial suggested effects on immune biomarkers and motor symptoms, but a charity summary calls it a small proof-of-concept trial whose findings need validation in larger trials. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
      "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41389828/",
      "also": [
        "https://cureparkinsons.org.uk/2026/02/results-from-the-phase-2-aza-pd-trial-are-now-published/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:14216d4f8e724f34fcf9c6cca3fda04aed42cbc71a5a6c7fbf2a6edbb52f2367",
        "ev:67b3595d1820f27c4f35723a89e953fd9d7c9cd34e0072780996d81a5af814dd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:701774f4012e48d218aa551bcb787b3a2a9389a2833df1213b6b9ccd66199ae3",
      "text": "Reviews report that minocycline, which reduces microglial activation and shows therapeutic effects in PD animal models, was not progressed to phase 3 and failed to show significant therapeutic efficacy in a Phase II clinical trial. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11492043/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12916702/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:cbd8439fc680ce0ad0571f995ef3a19e32a0c6ab998d2d87e55cb6408c4b420f",
        "ev:f30aa7ed63edb12b4a665cdb34b899a38e4d1a0a48db7720011ac7cbefeeca94"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:2ad1dabf9346b57c44352f6a7c926792da479b1278c13bf61c96b22ad3ebc2d8",
      "text": "A review and a Michael J. Fox Foundation grant summary both frame selecting trial participants by inflammatory phenotype or neuroinflammation-related PD subtype as a route to better trial success. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11492043/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.michaeljfox.org/grant/assessing-inhibition-nlrp3-reduce-brain-inflammation-parkinsons-disease"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:683dc4368f5c3a2da403ef83da64cbc6c3b0fb147a9684ef1778b3e90bfff721",
        "ev:fe58197415f65d22093a649d0d6a6f31b5476918733ea811827e4011189f58a2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:08a31dd2c740634d51fa13b45b82bee571c4de25af139cab1415e8b3498f7bf7",
      "text": "A review states that microglia play dual roles in PD, phagocytosing and clearing \u03b1-syn aggregates while becoming dysfunctional due to aggregate overload, which drives their transition to a pro-inflammatory phenotype. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12916702/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:ff219e2029efba0ea797d5c452c91f77fa58738aacf9712cbc1f27925fa303fa"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "narrative": [
    {
